From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:26:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [DS4.1] sample runtime loops and classify networking exchange
 phases

Base: candidate-38 series on upstream 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 (tree c061e5f6931306fa4655ba531428f639c365bf10).

Rationale: bias and slot-mapping loops need finite sampled event counts; sparknet exchange staging and doorbells need explicit phase labels. Runtime while loops keep their test and use a saturating observation counter. Profiling off has no change; profiling on adds only observation state, with first-iteration sampling for runtime loops.

Tests: 15 CPU phase-pass cases pass; candidate-38 series freshly applied and reproduced its tree; GPU validation recorded separately in the deployment experiment. Upstream status: local experiment, not submitted.
